{
  "dom_id": "step-q53554",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/43818f663454fe239d4b881a7cbd2f469391e80d87246a145f0fe1d294c9f71a.png)\n\nWhat length of chain will perfectly wrap around a circular tree trunk with a diameter of $2\\,\\text{yd}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The length of the chain needed to wrap around the tree is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=2\\,\\text{yd}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 2=2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}.\n$$",
